# Fork Strategy — Project Rule

This is a **fork of chatwoot/chatwoot**. Branch discipline is mandatory:

| Branch | Remote | Purpose |
|--------|--------|---------|
| `develop` | `origin/develop` = `upstream/develop` | Exact mirror of the original project — **no custom commits** |
| `main` | `origin/main` | All fork-specific changes, features, and fixes |

## Branch Workflow

**Never commit custom work on `develop`.** All agent and developer changes go on `main`.

### Sync develop with upstream (keep identical)

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout develop
git reset --hard upstream/develop
git push origin develop --force-with-lease
```

### Apply custom changes (always on main)

```bash
git checkout main
# make changes, commit here
git push origin main
```

### Bring upstream updates into main

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout develop && git reset --hard upstream/develop
git checkout main
git rebase develop   # or merge develop if preferred
git push origin main
```

## Change Rules

1. Minimize edits to upstream files
2. Prefer `custom/` overlay when possible
3. Mark every divergent line: `# FORK:` (Ruby) or `// FORK:` (JS/Vue)
4. Keep changes self-contained and grep-able: `rg "FORK:"`
5. Never add business logic in `app/`, `lib/`, or `enterprise/` without `FORK:` markers

## Prefer Data Over Code

- `InstallationConfig` for global flags
- `Account#enable_features` / `custom_attributes` for per-account flags
- Feature flags via Featurable concern

## Merge Safety

- Use `git rebase develop` on `main` after syncing develop
- When upstream changes conflict, grep FORK markers and reapply minimal deltas
- Follow all conflict-avoidance techniques in `fork-merge-conflicts.mdc`
